The unit-literal construction defect is repaired in generator version 2.0.1. Before editing, exact q-71722 parameters {'2':1,'3':4} and the negative-unit counterpart reproduced the reported exception. The construction rule now keeps distinct sign-preserving entry permutations and supplements undersized banks with single-entry coefficient/constant magnitude-reading errors. It preserves valid repeated values instead of excluding them. Every controlled bank retains the same sign/zero mask, preventing the earlier negative-corner/sign-pattern cue. The ordinary sampler is unchanged.

Fidelity: checks/regression.py passes all ten supplied complete source banks, including the previously restored moderate profiles, with 50 choices and 40 distractors. Prior signed-role/shortcut repairs pass 160 ordinary examples and 32 controlled records. All three historical findings have executable declarations in repair-regressions.json.

Correctness: checks/unit_regression.py independently parses the displayed systems, five choices and worked-solution stages for 63 affected-family cases across all ten profiles. Tests include the exact positive/negative units, repeated units and nonunits, signed endpoints, adjacent controls and fixed-evidence counterfactuals. A deliberately corrupted key fails the oracle. Fully collapsed unit systems allow direct recognition of implicit coefficients; that is a valid simplification of coefficient reading, and these cases remain supported.

Grading: the real native learner grader accepted 96 correct selections and rejected 384 wrong selections with zero unresolved outcomes. This is 480 response checks over source replays, affected inputs and a small ordinary sample, including intentionally repeated counterfactual baselines. No engine change was made.

Decision variation and delivery: all 43 easy and 20 moderate affected records survive the shared publisher filter. Independent math, within-profile sign/corner/position and scalar-extreme probes give the same results before and after filtering. No tested incidental cue universally identifies the answer within a source profile. Relevant coefficient changes update prompts, keys and explanations together and are covered by native grades. The ordinary five-question batch's complete question objects are unchanged and all five survive filtering. Finite shortcut probes are evidence against the named strategies, not proof against every possible cue. Actual learner history, reservations and policy weights are unavailable; no realized frequency claim is made.

Rendering and packaging: six actual Learning.html previews pass and all six screenshots were visually inspected. Matrices, augmentation dividers, signed unit notation and organized equations are legible and consistent; no clipping, missing content or broken math was observed. Manifest-only relocation passes both supported bands with exact deterministic output. Dependencies remain Python 3.13.5 and standard library only; the package still declares exactly three runtime files. Hard is unsupported.

Inventory: all seven captured generated records were reconstructed with their original complete content, identities and generation metadata, then compared against inventory read-only. None has a permutation orbit below five, so no stored case of the latest construction defect was demonstrated in the fully tested generated inventory. All seven earlier sign-shortcut findings remain recorded. Original assessed sources were excluded. affected-inventory.json is saved in this workspace and evidence/; its evidence_path values resolve relative to the supplied author-2 evidence_root as ../workspace/evidence/generated-records.json. This permits all writes to remain in the authorized workspace. No images were published and no database or other job was changed.

